The Org KPI management suite provides centralized data entry and governance. (1) Key Normalization: 'nk' (lowercase+trim+collapse-whitespace) is a CLIENT-SIDE JS Map key only — never used in SQL. DB joins use indexed (category_id, kra_name, kpi_name, review_period, review_year). (2) Progress Scoping: Dashboard metrics scope to selected data owner. (3) State Sync: 'OrgKpiEntryCard' merges sub_factors+achieved_value into UI state guarded by 'isDirtyRef'. (4) Save Integrity: Save handler permits sub_factors save with null achieved_value via strict undefined checks. (5) Auditing: 'is_org_kpi_audit_employee' grants org-wide auditor visibility. (6) Atomic Propagation (v2.66.0): 'propagate_org_kpi_value' RPC returns {propagated_count, skipped_count, skipped[]}. (7) Pre-flight Preview (v2.66.1): 'preview_org_kpi_propagation' + 'PropagationPreviewDialog'. (8) Reviewer Revision Flow (v2.66.2): SendBackDialog calls 'request_org_kpi_revision' for org-level KPIs. (9) Two-Trigger Insertion Pipeline (v2.66.3 + v2.66.6): (a) BEFORE INSERT 'trg_autoinherit_org_level_on_kpi_insert' (flag 'enable_org_kpi_auto_inherit', default ON) inherits is_org_level+scope from sibling Org KPIs with same signature, (b) AFTER INSERT 'trg_autopull_propagated_org_kpi' (flag 'enable_org_kpi_autopull') pre-fills review_submissions and advances to self_review. Audit: ORG_KPI_AUTO_INHERITED, ORG_KPI_AUTOPULLED_FOR_LATE_JOINER. (10) Scope Change Cascade + OKV Migration (v2.66.5 + v2.66.7): 'useChangeOrgKpiScope' calls RPC 'change_org_kpi_scope_cascading' with 'current_only' or 'current_and_future'. v2.66.7 adds frequency awareness: detects KPI frequency and uses 'resolve_terminal_period()' to map every requested period to its cycle's terminal month (Bi-Monthly/Quarterly/Half-Yearly/Yearly), de-duplicating forward cascade so each cycle is touched once. Audit metadata records 'cycle_anchor=true' + 'frequency'. 'OrgKpiScopeChangeDialog' shows amber banner when editing multi-month KPIs. Helper 'migrate_okv_on_scope_change' handles 6-way matrix (aggregating AVG-collapses, splitting seeds 'draft' OKVs). Originals archived in 'okv_migration_history'. Audit action 'ORG_KPI_SCOPE_CASCADED'. (11) Inheritance Reconciler (v2.66.6): RPC 'reconcile_org_kpi_inheritance(p_dry_run)' bulk-promotes pre-existing KPIs that should already have inherited Org-level. UI in Data Repair as 'OrgKpiInheritanceReconciler'. Audit 'ORG_KPI_INHERITANCE_RECONCILED'. (12) Forward-Sync Trigger (v2.66.7): AFTER UPDATE trigger 'trg_sync_org_status_to_future_open_periods' on 'public.kpis' (flag 'enable_org_kpi_forward_sync', default ON) — when an admin promotes (false→true) or demotes (true→false) a KPI's 'is_org_level' or changes 'org_level_scope', mirrors that change to all sibling KPIs (same category_id+kra_name+kpi_name+employee_id) in future open periods. Locked periods (review_period_locks lock_type IN global/full) are skipped. Demotions additionally delete orphan 'draft' rows in org_kpi_values for those future periods. Every sync audit-logged as 'ORG_KPI_FORWARD_SYNCED' with from/to org_level, from/to scope, source_kpi_id, source/target period+year, orphan_okv_deleted count, system_action=true. Three governance flags now live in OrgKpiGovernanceSettings: enable_org_kpi_auto_inherit, enable_org_kpi_autopull, enable_org_kpi_forward_sync. (13) Submission Snapshot Immutability (v2.66.7.3, POLICY §88): Propagation COPIES achieved_value into each per-employee review_submissions row by-value, NOT by FK to org_kpi_values. This is intentional immutability per HR audit law — admin edits to the OKV source row must NOT silently mutate already-approved historical scores. Re-propagation must be an explicit, audit-logged action. (14) Per-KPI Audit Granularity (v2.66.7.3, POLICY §89): ORG_KPI_PROPAGATED audit rows are emitted per-KPI (one row per affected kpi_id), required by KpiTimeline, KpiJourneySection, and repair-stepped-back-siblings recovery engine. Bulk-summary rows may be added alongside but never replace per-KPI rows. (15) Re-propagation Toast Classification (v2.66.8, POLICY §88.1): When propagate_org_kpi_value returns propagated_count=0 with skip reason 'not_in_kra_set' (employees already self-reviewed), the toast MUST be informational ("Already propagated"), NOT destructive. Only 'kpi_not_found' and 'race_lost_during_advance' deserve red destructive toasts. Per-scope batch loops in OrgKpiDataEntry.executeSaveAndPropagate MUST pass 'silent: true' to each mutateAsync and emit ONE summary toast at the end — never N stacked toasts.
 (16) Fact-Based Tile Status (ADR-055, v2.66.11): Org KPI Data Entry tile chip ("Pending/Entered/Propagated/Stuck") MUST combine org_kpi_values.status with the real per-employee kpis.status — never OKV.status alone. If every mapped child has advanced past kra_set (kraSetEmpIds.size === 0 && mappedEmpIds.size > 0), the tile is propagated regardless of stale OKV (draft/sent_back). useOrgLevelKpisWithEmployees returns mappedEmpIdsByKey for this. Tests: src/test/orgKpiTileStatus.test.ts.
